{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/568831-fallenblooded","id":568831,"title":"Fallenblooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-25T23:26:38-07:00","id":568831,"title":"Fallenblooded","content":"So the much anticipated demon conversion guide came out as I'm sure everyone in this subforum has noticed.<br /> <br /> Something beyond its scope is the children of the fallen, which were mentioned but never actually written up in dtf.<br /> <br /> Has anyone brainstormed over how they'd handle those demonspawn in a nwod dtf game or hybrid game?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T00:26:01-07:00","id":568885,"title":"","content":"There is a problem with those at least fluffwise. in the days of fire they are mentioned and there they were monsters that were almost not stopable by the fallen themselves during their height during the great war. <br /> You could try to simulate them using the heirs for hell rule, but if you take the fluff......they should have access to the full powers of the demons (else they are not as strong as the fluff suggests)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T03:16:39-07:00","id":568960,"title":"","content":"How is that a problem? Templates can be as powerful as you want them to be.<br /> <br /> As for having the full powers of demons, equal power levels doesn't mean identical powers.<br /> <br /> In Judgement day there's an option for Lucifer to teach humanity how to harness their faith to cancel out demonic powers, the demonspawn of dtf might have similar abilities, or ways to channel faith entirely different from either the fallen or humanity. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T02:32:58-07:00","id":571092,"title":"","content":"Possibly use the Lucifuge &quot;template&quot; with Fallen's trappings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T03:24:40-07:00","id":571139,"title":"","content":"Certainly a possibility, although my natural inclination is to make the nephilim stronger than the lucifuge. For one thing, it seems appropriate for a first gen to have more mojo, and second of all I wouldn't want a forced crossover here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","nam